  "interpretation": "Breaking exact arm symmetry removes the trivial three-bit-code equivalence. The repaired pairwise heuristic is still not enough: on this six-way task it greedily chooses a set with much poorer final localization than a planner that scores the actual multi-hypothesis Gaussian classification objective. The latter reaches about 84% accuracy with three soma-only trials, above the roughly 76.5% mean of matched-budget random designs and well above three individual probes. This is a stronger design benchmark, but it still assumes the forward models and noise are correct; nuisance uncertainty/model mismatch remain the next mandatory attacker."
